  "summary": "A distinctive jewelry style where silver sheets are soldered together to create raised designs on oxidized backgrounds.",
  "description": "This technique involves soldering a design cut from a silver sheet onto a base sheet of silver, which is then oxidized to create contrast. The aesthetic emerged in the mid-20th century as Hopi silversmiths developed their own distinctive style separate from Zuni and Navajo traditions.",
